      ],
      "line": "Under the red paint, older paint: a masked face, and the words THE KING OF FALLEN THINGS, a play in five parts.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        16,
        10
      ],
      "line": "A trunk of costumes, every one let out and taken in a dozen times, and a crown of painted wood.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "line": "A playbill nailed to the wagon's side, the town names crossed out one by one as the gates took them.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        19,
        8
      ],
      "line": "The oxen are dyed red at the horns, for luck, or for show."
    }
  ],
  "people": [
    {
      "name": "Fen the herb-wife",
      "unit": "town_trader",
      "cell": [
        9,
        6
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 1,
      "chatter": [
        "Redcap from the verges, frostmoss from the north road. I pick what you walk past.",
        "Three herbs make a draught, or two over a good fire. Two and a redcap make a better one. You're welcome."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "Herbs, love? Fresh off the road, which is fresher than off a shelf.",
          "You look like you've been fighting. Everybody looks like they've been fighting this year."
        ],
        "again": "Back for more green?",
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "Where do you pick them?",
            "a": "Off the verges as we go. The land grows them if you know where to look: under hedges, by water, in the cold."
          }
        ],
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "herbs",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "redcap",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "frostmoss",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "red_draught"
          }
        ],
        "shop": "Picked this week. Mostly.",
        "sold": "Steep it, don't boil it.",
        "bye": "Break a leg. Not really."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Big Aldo the cook",
      "unit": "innkeeper",
      "cell": [
        13,
        9
      ],
      "facing": [
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 1,
      "chatter": [
        "Sit. Eat. Nobody leaves the Red Wagons hungry, it's in the contract.",
        "Stew. It was a rabbit this morning. It's a stew now. That's the whole play."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": "Hungry? Course you are. Sit.",
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "bread",
            "restock": true
          }
        ],
        "shop": "Bread from the morning bake, wrapped against the dust.",
        "sold": "Eat it warm.",
        "bye": "Come back hungry."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Perrin, who played the king",
      "unit": "drunk_elf",
      "cell": [
        16,
        6
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "'I was a king of fallen things, and I fell with them.' Act five. Nobody stays for act five.",
        "We played Stormreach once. They threw roses. Well. They threw something."
      ]
    }
